id=axion_spsm
name=Axion Super Power Saving
version=v3.10.0
versionCode=77
author=Axion SPSM
description=v3.10.0, the measurement round + gesture navigation: a device census (6,354 calls in 488s of real use) showed the cost is churn, not any single call - every short screen-off re-ran the per-app deep passes (~48 passes in 8 minutes at a 15s timeout, ~100 binder calls each, every one a JVM start). deep_grace_secs (default 75, 0 restores the old behavior) defers the per-app restrictions until the screen has really stayed off, killing ~90% of those passes. Native cmd paths (settings/activity/package) replace the JVM wrappers with the old commands as fallback. spsm-tool.jar runs a whole batch in ONE JVM - the exit’s 187 unstop calls included - proven byte-equivalent to the fan by the suite, falling back to it on any doubtful answer. And the bottom edge becomes Axion’s: spsm-gesturemon, a native evdev recognizer started with the mode (swipe up = Axion home, hold = Axion recents, zero CPU between touches, no grab - normal touches unaffected), gated on the phone being in gesture mode AND the launcher actually being blocked by the mode; a gesture phone keeps its gestures for the session, every other phone gets the proven three-button path. Every old path stays as the fallback. On-phone benchmark round pending - see docs/RELEASE-v3.10.0.md.